WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.340
This is a production of Cornell University

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:11.860
Welcome to Cornell University's online Cornell&nbsp;
garden-based learning courses. We are thrilled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:17.020
about your interest in one or more of our&nbsp;
courses. Please take a few moments to watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:23.470
this video which outlines several important&nbsp;
details. These courses are designed for adult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:28.990
learners who wish to expand their knowledge of&nbsp;
the topic often for their own enrichment. As with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:34.660
most online or autonomous learning situations&nbsp;
students typically get out what they put into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:41.950
the course. The courses are non-accredited and are&nbsp;
designed for non-matriculated students. So you do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:47.050
not have to be enrolled at Cornell University and&nbsp;
the course does not count towards college credit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:52.660
We find that the most successful students are&nbsp;
those who are intrinsically motivated to complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:58.780
readings and assignments to devote considerable&nbsp;
time to coursework and to communicate with your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.450
classmates freely and often in an effort to&nbsp;
get the most from this course. We welcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:09.820
participants from around the world and find that&nbsp;
international students at a unique perspective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:16.630
to the course environment. Each course is catered&nbsp;
toward a different skill level. Please review the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.890
course syllabus for the course you are interested&nbsp;
in to learn about the target audience for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:27.100
specific course. For example, Organic Gardening&nbsp;
is designed for beginners while Botanical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:32.260
Illustration 3 - Advanced Techniques is designed&nbsp;
for those with greater mastery of the subject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:39.430
area. The courses are fully online and students&nbsp;
should have a basic knowledge of how to use a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:45.550
computer and have an openness around learning the&nbsp;
technology. It is not necessary to have previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:51.070
experience with taking online courses. Students&nbsp;
will have access to the course interface for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:56.290
time frame of the course. Much like a traditional&nbsp;
classroom in which once you leave the room and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.940
the course is over when this course is finished&nbsp;
you are responsible for keeping any records you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:07.600
wish since the course is cleared or reset for the&nbsp;
next group of participants. Students who complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.340
all assignments will receive a certificate of&nbsp;
completion at the conclusion of the course.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:19.410
Though specific supplies will vary for each course&nbsp;
students must have a computer with high-speed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:25.260
access. Some courses also require a device for&nbsp;
scanning particular assignment submissions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:33.000
Please listen carefully to our refund policy.&nbsp;
If you choose to withdraw any time prior to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.520
end of the introductory period before the start&nbsp;
of Lesson One you can receive a refund MINUS a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:44.910
one hundred and fifty dollar processing fee.&nbsp;
This fee applies to each course dropped. Once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:51.300
week one has begun we are unable to provide you&nbsp;
with a refund. Given that this course demands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.890
a significant amount of time, attention,&nbsp;
and energy over an extended period of time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:00.480
it is important to take steps in advance of the&nbsp;
program to ensure that you have the necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:07.170
support structures in place. The estimated time&nbsp;
commitment varies for each online course. Please&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:11.760
review the course syllabus for the course you are&nbsp;
interested in to learn about the estimated hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:19.230
per week. Most courses are six to eight weeks and&nbsp;
offer a blend of online and hands-on learning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:25.620
Each week's lessons will contain a combination&nbsp;
of selected readings, activities to carry out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:32.280
at home, reflective writing, student discussion&nbsp;
forum prompts, and optional additional readings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.830
activities and resources. Students submit&nbsp;
their weekly assignments before the stated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:43.800
deadline and the instructor provides timely&nbsp;
feedback. Though the class is not live,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.620
participants are expected to keep up with the&nbsp;
weekly assignments and discussions. Because the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:55.470
weekly topics build on each other, skipping a&nbsp;
topic one week will cause some confusion. It is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:01.590
a requirement to engage in at least a full page&nbsp;
of reflective writing weekly. While some students&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:07.530
initially balk at this, most appreciate how with&nbsp;
time the reflection helps to deepen their course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:13.710
experience. As John Dewey so famously said,&nbsp;
"We do not just learn from our experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:20.730
But we learn from reflecting on it." The student&nbsp;
discussion forum is a way to share resources and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:26.190
get to know one another. Although sharing your&nbsp;
work with others is not required, some students&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:32.010
also appreciate the chance to offer their work&nbsp;
for celebration and feedback from others. Open&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:37.680
dialog is encouraged between the instructor and&nbsp;
students. Students are encouraged to contact their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.740
course instructor with any questions. Some courses&nbsp;
have an introductory period before the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:49.950
of week one. This is a time for students to gain&nbsp;
access, become familiar with the course interface,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:55.920
and practice doing a few simple tasks -- such as&nbsp;
posting an introduction in the student discussion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:01.470
forum. Successful students take time during the&nbsp;
introductory period to carefully read all course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:08.040
materials and become familiar with the nuances of&nbsp;
the course offering. If you are taking drawing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:13.560
watercolor, or the advanced techniques botanical&nbsp;
illustration course, it is much better to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:19.440
spend a shorter period of time each day on your&nbsp;
assignments then to power through an occasionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.450
four or five hour chunks of time. You will want&nbsp;
to devote at least 12 to 15 hours per week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:30.450
and with increasing hours you will gain more&nbsp;
proficiency. You'll grow much more in scale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:36.000
with more sessions and in addition stay on top of&nbsp;
the assignments. Though the assignments are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.650
difficult -- in fact they can be enjoyable&nbsp;
and relaxing -- there are many of them. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:47.190
is important to keep your expectations modest.&nbsp;
These are just six-week courses. And remember the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:54.810
10,000-hours rule of thumb: It takes a long time&nbsp;
to gain mastery. If you have additional questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.810 --> 00:06:00.060
please review our frequently asked questions&nbsp;
page. If you are unable to find an answer there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:05.100
then please email the relevant point of&nbsp;
contact for the course in question. Thank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.490
you for watching this video and we hope&nbsp;
to see you in one of our future course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:17.040
offerings. This has been a production of&nbsp;
Cornell University on the web at cornell edu

